{
  "name": "l0_keyvalues_tree",
  "about": "The KeyValues file reader FUN_101f2180 (0x101f2180) from its parse loop on (the file arms R1..R6 are the loader's), with the target node FUN_101f2e20 names after the file (ECX at 0x101f218b), and the recursive block parser FUN_101f2360 (0x101f2360) over the token wrapper FUN_101f2f30 (0x101f2f30). Roots: a key then `{` (0x10547B78); L3a reuses the target (Clear 0x101f2c60, SetName 0x101f2090), L3b makes a new root chained through 0x101f2cd0; a missing brace is `ERROR: parsing KeyValue in file %s, expecting {, got {` (the constant, not the token) and the node is reused for the next key; a top-level `}` is an ordinary root key; a blank text returns 1 with the target untouched. Blocks: `}` (0x10547B64) or an empty key (a quoted \"\" too) closes; every child is appended in file order; `{` recurses; a leaf is interned (0x101f2f70) and, unquoted, typed by _strtol (0x104319A8, base 10, clamping) against _strtod (0x1043190E, VC6 ___strgtold12: no hex, no inf/nan): strtod consuming more -> type 3 float, strtol consuming nothing -> type 1, else type 2 int; a quoted leaf stays type 1. A value missing before a brace takes the brace as its text. Reported as `fail`, a root arm, a leaf type or value, an error line or the root chain differs from retail's.",
